_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"Frequency (Hz)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The  responses  of  the  system  correspond  to  1DOF oscillators and using a least square estimation we obtained the values of the mechanical parameters. Those values are given in Table 1 with respect to the parameters given by the manufacturer.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":264.84743468689896,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64095999999998,"r":288.7189200000001,"t":319.8820946484375},"charspan":[0,246],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/26","text":"The  responses  of  the  system  correspond  to  1DOF oscillators and using a least square estimation we obtained the values of the mechanical parameters. Those values are given in Table 1 with respect to the parameters given by the manufacturer."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.3 Modal parameters","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":235.69563492348652,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.650919999999985,"r":161.67911999999998,"t":245.4609746484374},"charspan":[0,20],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/27","text":"3.3 Modal parameters"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The developed method requires an external possibility of making the shaker vibrate and is quite difficult to apply to  larger  shakers.  In  this  case,  modal  analysis  is  an alternative since the mechanical  parameters  and  the modal ones are equivalent to characterize the system.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":170.366874686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.65091999999997,"r":288.6292799999999,"t":225.31189464843737},"charspan":[0,286],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/28","text":"The developed method requires an external possibility of making the shaker vibrate and is quite difficult to apply to  larger  shakers.  In  this  case,  modal  analysis  is  an alternative since the mechanical  parameters  and  the modal ones are equivalent to characterize the system."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"In  this  section,  a  short  review  of  the  modal  theory will be presented to sufficiently master this equivalence as the relationship between movement, global coordinates, modal coordinates, and modal parameters.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":124.39151468689897,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.65091999999999,"r":288.53964,"t":167.7829346484374},"charspan":[0,217],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/29","text":"In  this  section,  a  short  review  of  the  modal  theory will be presented to sufficiently master this equivalence as the relationship between movement, global coordinates, modal coordinates, and modal parameters."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 1. Mechanical parameters","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":759.572314686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":360.67,"r":489.42640000000006,"t":768.5120946484375},"charspan":[0,30],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"Table 1. Mechanical parameters"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"a For  testing  purposes,  the  original  vibrating  table  is  equipped with an extra 16 g fastening bolt.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":563.7887002253606,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.044,"r":540.875,"t":583.2278146484375},"charspan":[0,107],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"a For  testing  purposes,  the  original  vibrating  table  is  equipped with an extra 16 g fastening bolt."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.3.1 Theoretical aspects","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":534.9574779750908,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.05,"r":423.57008,"t":544.4111746484375},"charspan":[0,25],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/32","text":"3.3.1 Theoretical aspects"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label"